title: "G1 Lifecycle and presence: SteamVR, units, the session, pause for VR games, worn, display power (78e93b1, G1Lifecycle.tla)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    direction LR
    lg0: Off, down, or nothing held
    lg1: Running, shown, worn
    lg2: Between: starting, queued, waiting out a timer
    lg3: Paused, hidden, dark, or held
    lg4: Suspected open bug: the state that breaks the rule
    lg5: L1 open, PointerFreeWhilePaused: a relay restart forgets the 3D pointer the helper still holds, pause cannot let it go (red L1.1-6)
    lg6: L2 open, HandsOffWhilePaused: a desktop that starts during a pause starts camd + hands (red L2.1-6, no crash needed)
    lg7: L3 open, HandsFollowDesktop: a resume job starts camd + hands with SteamVR off (red L3.1-7)
    lg8: L4 open, GazeOffWhilePaused: is-active misses a restarting ft-gazed, systemd brings it back mid-pause (red L4.1-6)
    lg9: L5 open, GazeBackAfterResume + ClosedDesktopComesBack: a relay restart before the resume job loses the stopped list (red L5.1-7)
    lg10: L6 open, NoStuckGamePause: a relay restart while the game ends leaves Frametop paused (red L6.1-8)
    lg11: Hold in every config: 3D mouse + gamepad let go on pause, desktop matches pause, worn agrees within 1.5 s, dark displays have an owner, away lets go
    lg12: L7, sensitivity, not red: one lost "pause off" datagram leaves the panels hidden (ft-screens' pause is sticky)
    lg13: Another group: arrows into it are what G1 triggers there, labeled with that group
    lg14: Drawn from the model's actions (27,172 to 34,942 states: too many to draw), badges from TLC's shortest paths
  }
